{"poe":"brief","content":"Planning Stage 1 (complete delivery) for Wordle Clone. Reading CONOPS and Must-Nots. No Guardrails Review artifact present — proceeding since Must-Nots are fully specified with no conflicts or open questions. Will decompose into Epics, Features, and Tasks covering game engine, UI, and quality assurance, then request specialist reviews before yielding."}
```

```json
{"poe":"step","name":"readiness-check","detail":"No guardrails-review.md artifact found. Must-Nots document is present and complete with 14 hard constraints across 7 categories, zero open questions. Treating as APPROVED — proceeding to scope definition."}
```

```json
{"poe":"step","name":"scope-definition","detail":"Identifying P0 features from CONOPS. This is a single-stage delivery — the full CONOPS is the MVP. All 4 objectives are P0: (1) playable in browser zero-dep, (2) color-coded feedback, (3) dictionary validation, (4) random word per load. Applying MMD: single static file set, independently deployable by double-click, observable value to Casual Player from day one."}
```

```json
{"poe":"step","name":"epic-creation","detail":"Creating Epic nodes for three capability areas: game engine, player interface, quality assurance."}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"e1","title":"Player can play a complete game with correct word selection and feedback","description":"Delivers the core game engine: embedded word corpus, random target word selection, dictionary validation, and color-coded feedback algorithm. sourcePersonas: Casual Player. userValue: Player receives accurate green/yellow/gray feedback enabling them to reason toward the answer.","skill":"frontend","type":"epic","parent_id":null,"depends_on":[]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"e2","title":"Player can interact with the game through a visual board and keyboard","description":"Delivers the full user interface: 6x5 tile grid, keyboard input capture, tile color rendering, and win/loss end-state messaging. sourcePersonas: Casual Player. userValue: Player sees the board, types guesses, and receives an outcome — fully playable without instruction.","skill":"frontend","type":"epic","parent_id":null,"depends_on":[]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"e3","title":"Implementation satisfies all Must-Nots and passes cross-browser verification","description":"Delivers quality assurance: unit tests for the color-coding algorithm (per MN-QG-02), must-not compliance audit across all 14 constraints, and senior engineer code review. sourcePersonas: Casual Player (indirectly). userValue: Confidence that the game is correct, private, dependency-free, and works on all target browsers.","skill":"senior-engineer","type":"epic","parent_id":null,"depends_on":["e1","e2"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"step","name":"feature-decomposition","detail":"Decomposing each Epic into independently testable Features."}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f1","title":"System can select a random five-letter target word from an embedded corpus","description":"Implements the word list as an inline JS array (answer pool + valid-guess dictionary) with a random selector. estimatedDays: 1. architectureRef: MN-ARCH-01 (no external files/CDNs), MN-ARCH-02 (no build step), MN-SEC-01 (no network fetch for word list).","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e1","depends_on":[]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f2","title":"System can validate a player's guess and reject invalid input","description":"Implements validation: rejects submissions with fewer than 5 letters (blocked, no attempt consumed) and words not in the dictionary (rejected, no attempt consumed per MN-TRUST-01). estimatedDays: 0.5. architectureRef: MN-TRUST-01, MN-TRUST-03 (target word fixed at game start, not re-selected on rejection).","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e1","depends_on":["f1"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f3","title":"System can score a guess with correct green/yellow/gray color logic","description":"Implements the Wordle scoring algorithm: greens resolved first, then yellows allocated to remaining unmatched letters only. Handles duplicate letters correctly per MN-QG-02. estimatedDays: 1. architectureRef: MN-QG-02.","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e1","depends_on":["f1"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f4","title":"Player can see a 6x5 tile grid that updates with each submitted guess","description":"Implements the HTML structure for the game board (6 rows × 5 tiles) and the rendering logic that fills tiles with letters and applies color classes after scoring. estimatedDays: 1. designSystemRef: tile colors (green #6aaa64, yellow #c9b458, gray #787c7e).","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e2","depends_on":["f3"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f5","title":"Player can type a guess using physical keyboard with live tile preview","description":"Implements keyboard event listeners (keydown): letter keys populate the current-row tiles, Backspace removes the last letter, Enter submits. Input is blocked after 5 letters or when game is over. estimatedDays: 0.5. architectureRef: MN-SEC-03 (no innerHTML with user input — use textContent).","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e2","depends_on":["f4"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f6","title":"Player sees a win or loss message when the game ends","description":"Implements end-game detection: win when guess matches target, loss when 6 attempts exhausted. Displays outcome message and reveals the answer on loss. Input locked after game ends. estimatedDays: 0.5. architectureRef: MN-TRUST-02 (answer only revealed in loss state), MN-TRUST-01 (attempt counter logic).","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e2","depends_on":["f5","f2"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f7","title":"Game is visually playable on both mobile and desktop browsers","description":"Implements responsive CSS: tile grid layout, letter sizing, color states (correct/present/absent), end-game banner. No on-screen keyboard needed (physical keyboard only). Must render correctly on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge. estimatedDays: 0.5.","skill":"frontend","type":"feature","parent_id":"e2","depends_on":["f4"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f8","title":"Color-coding algorithm is verified correct for duplicate-letter edge cases","description":"Implements unit tests (inline test runner or simple assertion script) covering: (a) repeated letter where only one instance is in word — only one yellow/green, (b) letter in correct position and also elsewhere — correct-position green, other gray. Required by MN-QG-02. estimatedDays: 0.5.","skill":"test","type":"feature","parent_id":"e3","depends_on":["f3"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"f9","title":"All 14 Must-Not constraints are verified against the shipped implementation","description":"Manual compliance audit: walks each MN-* item and verifies the verification criterion passes. Produces a pass/fail checklist. Any failure is a blocker. estimatedDays: 0.5.","skill":"test","type":"feature","parent_id":"e3","depends_on":["f5","f6","f7","f8"]}
```

