```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t1","title":"Create index.html skeleton with game board markup","description":"Produces: index.html with DOCTYPE, head (meta charset, viewport, title, inline or linked CSS), and body containing the 6×5 grid (div.board > div.row*6 > div.tile*5) and a message div for end-game. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 1. acceptanceCriteria: Opening index.html in a browser shows a blank grid layout with no JS errors in console; file:// protocol works.","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f4","depends_on":[]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t2","title":"Embed word corpus as inline JS arrays with random selector","description":"Produces: words.js (or inline <script>) containing WORDS array (valid guesses, ~2000+ words) and ANSWERS array (subset of common 5-letter words), plus a getRandomAnswer() function. No fetch, no import from CDN. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 2. acceptanceCriteria: getRandomAnswer() returns a 5-letter string from ANSWERS on every call; MN-SEC-01 satisfied (no network call); MN-ARCH-01 satisfied (no npm/build).","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f1","depends_on":[]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t3","title":"Implement isValidGuess(word) validation function","description":"Produces: isValidGuess(word) that returns false if word.length !== 5 or word not in WORDS array; returns true otherwise. Must not mutate game state. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 1. acceptanceCriteria: Returns false for 3-letter strings; returns false for 5-letter non-word; returns true for valid dictionary word; target word itself is always valid.","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f2","depends_on":["t2"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t4","title":"Implement scoreGuess(guess, target) color-coding algorithm","description":"Produces: scoreGuess(guess, target) returning array of 5 objects {letter, result} where result is 'correct'|'present'|'absent'. Algorithm: (1) mark all exact-position matches as 'correct' and remove from unmatched pool, (2) for remaining positions, mark 'present' if letter exists in unmatched pool (consuming the match), else 'absent'. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 2. acceptanceCriteria: scoreGuess('speed','speed') → all correct; scoreGuess('aabbc','abcde') handles duplicate correctly per MN-QG-02 cases; scoreGuess('crane','tiger') → all absent for non-matching letters.","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f3","depends_on":["t2"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t5","title":"Implement guess submission handler wiring validation and scoring to board state","description":"Produces: submitGuess() function that: (1) reads current row letters, (2) calls isValidGuess — if false, shakes row and returns, (3) calls scoreGuess, (4) updates board state array, (5) calls renderRow to display results, (6) increments attempt counter, (7) calls checkGameOver. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 2. acceptanceCriteria: Invalid word does not increment attempt counter (MN-TRUST-01); valid guess advances row; target word does not change between calls (MN-TRUST-03).","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f2","depends_on":["t3","t4","t1"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t6","title":"Implement renderRow(rowIndex, scoreResults) tile color update","description":"Produces: renderRow function that sets each tile's textContent to the letter (using textContent, not innerHTML, per MN-SEC-03) and adds CSS class 'correct'|'present'|'absent' to apply color. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 1. acceptanceCriteria: Green tiles show for correct letters; yellow for present; gray for absent; textContent used (not innerHTML assignment with user input); MN-SEC-03 satisfied.","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f4","depends_on":["t1","t5"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t7","title":"Implement keyboard event listener for letter input, Backspace, and Enter","description":"Produces: document.addEventListener('keydown') handler. Letter keys (A-Z): append to current row if fewer than 5 letters and game active. Backspace: remove last letter. Enter: call submitGuess(). Input ignored after game over. Uses textContent for tile updates. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 1. acceptanceCriteria: Typing 5 letters fills current row tiles; Backspace clears last; Enter triggers submission; typing beyond 5 letters is ignored; game-over locks input.","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f5","depends_on":["t1","t5"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t8","title":"Implement checkGameOver() win/loss detection and end-game message display","description":"Produces: checkGameOver(scoreResults, attemptCount) that: if all 5 results are 'correct' → show win message; if attemptCount === 6 and not won → show loss message with target word revealed. Message shown in .message div. Game state locked. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 1. acceptanceCriteria: Win message shown on correct guess; loss message reveals target word only after attempt 6 (MN-TRUST-02); no win/loss before those conditions; reloading page resets all state.","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f6","depends_on":["t5"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t9","title":"Implement responsive CSS for game board, tiles, and color states","description":"Produces: styles (inline in HTML or styles.css) covering: board centering, tile sizing (min 50px square), correct/present/absent color fills (#6aaa64, #c9b458, #787c7e on dark tile), readable letter text, responsive layout for mobile (viewport-width-based sizing), win/loss message styling. No external fonts or CDN. artifactType: code. estimatedHours: 1. acceptanceCriteria: Game visually playable on 375px mobile viewport; tiles clearly colored; no layout overflow; MN-SEC-02 satisfied (no external CSS).","skill":"frontend","type":"task","parent_id":"f7","depends_on":["t1"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t10","title":"Write unit tests for scoreGuess duplicate-letter edge cases","description":"Produces: test script (inline or separate test.js runnable in browser console or Node) asserting MN-QG-02 cases: (a) guess='spell' target='hello' — only one 'l' should be yellow/green not both; (b) guess='opens' target='prone' — verify correct-position letter is green, duplicate elsewhere is gray. Uses simple assert() or console.assert(). artifactType: test. estimatedHours: 2. acceptanceCriteria: All assertions pass; running the test file produces zero failures; duplicate-letter algorithm verified for both MN-QG-02 test vectors.","skill":"test","type":"task","parent_id":"f8","depends_on":["t4"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t11","title":"Execute must-not compliance audit against all 14 MN constraints","description":"Produces: written audit report (inline comment block or separate checklist) confirming pass/fail for each of MN-SEC-01 through MN-QG-02. Verification methods: Network tab check (MN-SEC-01), source inspection (MN-SEC-02, MN-SEC-03, MN-PRIV-01/02/03, MN-ARCH-01/02/03, MN-SCOPE-01/02), gameplay tests (MN-TRUST-01/02/03), cross-browser load (MN-QG-01). artifactType: test. estimatedHours: 2. acceptanceCriteria: All 14 MN items marked PASS; any FAIL is a blocker before review task.","skill":"test","type":"task","parent_id":"f9","depends_on":["t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]}
```

```json
{"poe":"task","id":"t12","title":"Senior engineer code review of complete implementation","description":"Produces: review findings covering correctness of game logic, MN compliance, code quality (no innerHTML user-input, no eval), file structure validity (opens via file://), and test coverage adequacy. artifactType: review. estimatedHours: 2. acceptanceCriteria: Review completed with explicit APPROVED or list of required changes; no Must-Not violations found; duplicate-letter logic confirmed correct.","skill":"senior-engineer","type":"task","parent_id":"e3","depends_on":["t11"]}
```

