{"poe":"step","name":"plan-validation","detail":"Validating coverage, must-not controls, test coverage, DAG acyclicity, assignability, and task sizing."}
```

Plan validation results:
- **Coverage**: All 4 CONOPS objectives covered: word selection (t2), validation (t3), color feedback (t4), win/loss (t8), UI (t1,t6,t7,t9)
- **Must-Nots requiring technical controls**: MN-SEC-01 (no fetch) → t2 acceptance criteria; MN-SEC-02 (no CDN) → t9; MN-SEC-03 (no innerHTML with user input) → t6,t7; MN-PRIV-01 (no storage) → t8 (no localStorage call); MN-TRUST-01 (invalid guess no attempt) → t5; MN-TRUST-02 (no early answer reveal) → t8; MN-TRUST-03 (target fixed) → t5; MN-ARCH-01/02/03 (vanilla JS, no build, no server) → t2 acceptance criteria; MN-QG-02 (duplicate letters) → t4+t10. All 14 MN items covered by audit t11.
- **Test coverage**: t4 (scoreGuess) → t10 (unit tests); all implementation → t11 (compliance audit)
- **DAG acyclicity**: All edges are strictly forward (t1→...→t12). No cycles.
- **Assignability**: frontend (t1–t9), test (t10–t11), senior-engineer (t12)
- **Right-sizing**: All tasks 1–2 hours. Largest tasks (t2: 2h embedding word list, t5: 2h wiring, t10: 2h tests, t11: 2h audit, t12: 2h review) are within the 4-hour ceiling.

