{"poe":"step","name":"review-requests","detail":"Requesting specialist plan reviews. Architecture review not required: no schema migrations, no Tauri commands, no new event types, no new subsystem boundaries — this is a static vanilla-JS client with no backend or protocol extensions."}
```

```json
{"poe":"review","reviewer_skill":"senior-engineer","id":"r-eng","content":"Stage 1 (complete delivery) plan for Wordle Clone — vanilla JS browser game.\n\n**Epics (3):**\n- e1: Game engine (word selection, validation, scoring) — skill: frontend\n- e2: Player UI (board, input, end-state) — skill: frontend\n- e3: Quality assurance (tests, compliance, review) — skill: senior-engineer\n\n**Features (9):**\n- f1: Word corpus + random selector (parent: e1)\n- f2: Guess validation — reject <5 letters or not-in-dict (parent: e1)\n- f3: scoreGuess() color algorithm with duplicate handling (parent: e1)\n- f4: 6x5 tile grid rendering (parent: e2)\n- f5: Keyboard input handler (parent: e2)\n- f6: Win/loss detection + end-game message (parent: e2)\n- f7: Responsive CSS (parent: e2)\n- f8: Unit tests for color algorithm (parent: e3)\n- f9: Must-not compliance audit (parent: e3)\n\n**Tasks (12):**\n- t1: HTML skeleton (frontend, ~1h) — parent: f4\n- t2: Embed word corpus as inline JS arrays (frontend, ~2h) — parent: f1\n- t3: isValidGuess() function (frontend, ~1h) — parent: f2\n- t4: scoreGuess() algorithm (frontend, ~2h) — parent: f3\n- t5: submitGuess() handler wiring validation+scoring to board (frontend, ~2h) — parent: f2\n- t6: renderRow() tile color update using textContent (frontend, ~1h) — parent: f4\n- t7: Keyboard event listener (frontend, ~1h) — parent: f5\n- t8: checkGameOver() win/loss + answer reveal (frontend, ~1h) — parent: f6\n- t9: Responsive CSS (frontend, ~1h) — parent: f7\n- t10: Unit tests for duplicate-letter edge cases (test, ~2h) — parent: f8\n- t11: Must-not compliance audit — all 14 MN items (test, ~2h) — parent: f9\n- t12: Senior engineer code review (senior-engineer, ~2h) — parent: e3\n\n**Dependency edges (19):**\nt2→t3, t2→t4, t1→t5, t3→t5, t4→t5, t1→t6, t5→t6, t1→t7, t5→t7, t5→t8, t1→t9, t4→t10, t5→t11, t6→t11, t7→t11, t8→t11, t9→t11, t10→t11, t11→t12\n\n**Key architectural decisions reflected in plan:**\n- All JS is vanilla (no frameworks, no build tools) — MN-ARCH-01/02\n- Word corpus embedded inline (no fetch, no CDN) — MN-SEC-01/02\n- textContent used for user-derived tile content (never innerHTML) — MN-SEC-03\n- No localStorage or external calls — MN-PRIV-01/02\n- Target word locked at game start (t2 called once on load, stored in closure) — MN-TRUST-03\n- Answer only revealed in checkGameOver() loss branch — MN-TRUST-02\n- scoreGuess algorithm: greens first, then yellows from remaining unmatched pool — MN-QG-02\n\n**Must-Not coverage:** All 14 MN items have explicit acceptance criteria or audit coverage in t11.\n\nPlease review for: correctness of task decomposition and sizing, adequate must-not controls, DAG validity, any missing tasks, and overall stage completeness."}
```

